nisha (DevEx): FYI new quickstart issue: if a dev runs the paginator with aggressive concurrency + a tiny token TTL, the client can trigger a "token+retry" stampede and hammer our quotas. Repro is fast.

nisha (DevEx): Repro steps:
1) Quickstart with PAGE_SIZE=40, CONCURRENCY=6
2) Set AUTH_TTL=2s locally
3) Scroll or request 20 pages quickly
4) Some requests 429 during auth refresh -> client retries whole page worker -> duplicates + quota spike

jun (QA): Reproduced. UI spinner never stopped, network tab showed the same cursor requested multiple times.

nisha (DevEx): Snippet from quickstart:
```
async function pageWorker(cursor) {
  while (cursor) {
    for (let att=0; att<3; att++) {
      try {
        let res = await client.list({cursor, limit: PAGE_SIZE});
        cursor = res.next;
        break;
      } catch (err) {
        if (err.code === 'UNAUTH') { await auth.refresh(); continue; }
        if (err.code === 'RATE_LIMIT') { await sleep(500 * 2**att); continue; }
        throw err;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

sam (SDK): The pattern is retry-at-worker-level. That makes multiple workers race and re-request the same cursor when retries overlap. Two quick fixes: move retries into the SDK http layer and add an in-process inflight map keyed by cursor.

leo (Platform): Also, when auth.refresh() runs, other retries should pause briefly (100-300ms) instead of immediately retrying. That reduces token-rotation amplification.

jun (QA): Network trace: 6 workers fired page=5 concurrently, 4 got 429, token rotated, then 2 succeeded, client appended duplicates. Rate limit alerts spiked.

ratelimiter-bot: [event] quota:table:items sample-quickstart exceeded soft limit 1m reqs/min at 2026-03-22T09:10:12Z

ci-bot: flaky test: quickstart/paginator.test failed on main twice; reproduces with AUTH_TTL=2s in CI container.

sam (SDK): Proposed short-term changes:
- implement requestWithRetry in SDK (request-level) and remove worker-level retry loops
- add X-Idempotency-Key for list calls (cursor+limit) so server can dedupe if it wants
- provide an optional inflight map in sample app to ensure only one in-flight request per cursor
- expose maxConcurrentPages knob defaulting to 2 in quickstart

leo (Platform): We'll also add a metric (client_retries_due_to_auth) and an alert, and recommend increasing token TTL in dev docs.

nisha (DevEx): UX ask: quickstart should detect repeat 429s and surface a friendly warning suggesting to lower concurrency or extend AUTH_TTL. New users think the platform is broken.

jun (QA): Quick local patch (moved retry to http wrapper + inflight map) reduced duplicate page calls and lowered rate-limit events from ~90/min to ~6/min. No more stuck spinner.

sam (SDK): Follow-ups: PR to add request-level retries + idempotency headers, update quickstart to use SDK retries only, add docs blurb. I'll open PRs and a small integration test that simulates token expiry + 429s.

nisha (DevEx): Thanks all, saving this thread as the onboarding incident. I'll update the quickstart README with the concurrency note and AUTH_TTL tip. :thumbsup:
